<BaseLayout title="About"><section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-signal">About</p><h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold text-ink">A notebook for careful security work.</h1><div class="prose mt-8"><p>Signal Surface is a personal cybersecurity research and engineering blog. It is a place to work through defensive design, explain difficult systems, and record approaches that are useful in practice.</p><p>The emphasis is on clear reasoning: what a control protects, where it falls short, and how to operate it safely. Articles are written for practitioners who value evidence, maintainability, and constraints over theatre.</p><p>This is a static publication. There are no accounts, trackers, comments, or hidden application services.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
